              AMOS MAXS DOOR HANDLER, written by Ari Tsironis, V0.20 Beta
                                       01-05-94



- There are two example files, "Test.AMOS" and "NewFiles.AMOS", both are 
  fairly simple and explanatory, "NewFiles.AMOS" has a liberal dosing of
  comments and is probably the best MAXS "NewFile" Lister written to date,
  while "Test.AMOS" puts most of the commands through their paces.

- Both files are PD and you can do what you like with them, I would request
  though that you don't just make a coupla' mods to the "NewFiles" door and
  release it as your own, as it was a non-trivial excercise that I don't want
  others taking complete credit for...
 
- There are also two executables, (the above files compiled), which can be
  checked out before you do a thing, just hook 'em up the normal way, ie
  through door function 34.   



AMOS DOOR INSTRUCTIONS
----------------------

1) INSTRUCTION: M_portopen


   SUMMARY:     Initialises AMOS Door ReplyPort, finds MAXS Door ControlPort
                and hooks the AMOS Door ReplyPort to MAXS Door ControlPort.

                MUST BE the first door instruction of ANY AMOS door for MAXS.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_portopen(NODE_NUMBER)

                NODE_NUMBER: integer,  0 = local node, 1-9 = remote nodes.
                RESULT:      integer,  0 = fatal error, >0 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     NODE_NUMBER = Val(Left$(Command Line$,1))
                ERROR = M_portopen(NODE_NUMBER)



2) INSTRUCTION: M_portclose


   SUMMARY:     Sends the END function to the MAXS Door ControlPort and
                deletes the AMOS Door ReplyPort.

                MUST BE the last door instruction of ANY AMOS door for MAXS.


   USAGE:       M_portclose

 
   EXAMPLE:     M_portclose
   


3) INSTRUCTION: M_bbstext


   SUMMARY:     Outputs a string of text, (including ANSI sequences and
                Auto Inserts), to the modem and local BBS screen.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_bbstext(TEXT$)

                TEXT$:  String,   can contain from 1 to 79 characters.
                RESULT: integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 1 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_bbstext("Whoa...t'is to laugh"+chr$(13))



4) INSTRUCTION: M_localtext


   SUMMARY:     Outputs a string of text, (including ANSI sequences and
                Auto Inserts), only to the local BBS screen.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_localtext(TEXT$)

                TEXT$:  String,   can contain from 1 to 79 characters.
                RESULT: integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 2 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_localtext("Is that a canoe in your pocket?"+chr$(13))



5) INSTRUCTION: M_modemchar


   SUMMARY:     Outputs one char to the modem, ie remote.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_modemchar(CHAR)

                CHAR:  Integer, Any character from 0 to 255.
                RESULT: integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 3 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_modemchar(12)



5) INSTRUCTION: M_screenchar


   SUMMARY:     Outputs one char to the local screen, ie local.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_screenchar(CHAR)

                CHAR:  Integer, Any character from 0 to 255.
                RESULT: integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 4 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_screenchar(13)



6) INSTRUCTION: M_bbschar


   SUMMARY:     Outputs one char to both the modem and the local screen.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_bbschar(CHAR)

                CHAR:  Integer, Any character from 0 to 255.
                RESULT: integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 5 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_bbschar(8)



7) INSTRUCTION: M_prompttext


   SUMMARY:     Displays a text message and prompts for a CR terminated input
                string.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_prompttext(TEXT$,INPUT$)

                TEXT$:  String,   can contain from 1 to 79 characters.
                INPUT$: String,   length determines how many characters can be
                                  input.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 6 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     TEXT$ = "Bugger Orf"
                INPUT$ = Space$(10)
                CARRIER = M_prompttext(TEXT$,INPUT$)



8) INSTRUCTION: M_sprompttext


   SUMMARY:     Displays a text message and prompts for a CR terminated input
                string, allows "stacked commands" for Paragon compatability.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_sprompttext(TEXT$,INPUT$)

                TEXT$:  String,   can contain from 1 to 79 characters.
                INPUT$: String,   length determines how many characters can be
                                  input.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 7 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     TEXT$ = "Luscious Loser"
                INPUT$ = Space$(20)
                CARRIER = M_sprompttext(TEXT$,INPUT$)



9) INSTRUCTION: M_getchar


   SUMMARY:     Displays a text message and waits for a single key press.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_getchar(TEXT$,CHAR$)

                TEXT$:  String,   can contain from 1 to 79 characters.
                CHAR$:  String,   contains either ASCII char as first char, or
                                  ANSI sequence representing key.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 8 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     TEXT$ = "Smash that keyboard Bubba..."
                CHAR$ = Space$(8)
                CARRIER = M_getchar(TEXT$,CHAR$)



10)INSTRUCTION: M_twituser


   SUMMARY:     Spontaneous Idiot Removal, (SIR. TM)


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_twituser

                RESULT: Integer,  20 = already dropped carrier, 9 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_twituser



11)INSTRUCTION: M_showfile


   SUMMARY:     Displays a text/ANSI file.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_showfile(FILE$)

                FILE$:  String,   File name of displayable file.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 10 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_showfile("BBS:Text/idiot.text")



12)INSTRUCTION: M_checkfile


   SUMMARY:     Checks to see if a file is online.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_checkfile(FILE$)

                FILE$:  String,   File name of online file.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, else file status.


   EXAMPLE:     STATUS = M_checkfile("BBS:Files/idjut.lha")



13)INSTRUCTION: M_editfile


   SUMMARY:     Edits a text file, (I can't make it work!).


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_editfile(FILE$)

                FILE$:  String,   File name of editable file.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier else file status.


   EXAMPLE:     STATUS = M_editfile("BBS:Text/BBS.text")



14)INSTRUCTION: M_getusernum(TYPE)


   SUMMARY:     Retrieves some MAXS and Paragon integer based information
                for the current user.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_getusernum(TYPE)

                TYPE:   Integer,  Type of info to obtain.
                                  1: Access Level.
                                  2: Expert Mode, (Paragon).
                                  3: Net Credits, (Paragon).
                                  4: Number of Calls.
                                  5: Calls to System.
                                  6: Graphics Mode.
                                  7: Minutes Remaining.
                                  8: Screen Columns.
                                  9: Screen Rows.

                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, else TYPE RESULT.


   EXAMPLE:     ACCESS = M_getusernum(1)



15)INSTRUCTION: M_getuserstr(TYPE,USER$)


   SUMMARY:     Retrieves some MAXS and Paragon string based information
                for the current user.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_getuserstr(TYPE,USER$)

                TYPE:   Integer,  Type of info to obtain.
                                  1: Name.
                                  2: Password.
                                  3: Suburb.
                                  4: City, (Paragon).
                                  5: State (Paragon).
                                  6: Zip Code, (Paragon).
                                  7: Doors Path.
                                  8: BBS Path.
                                  9: Date.
                                 10: Time.
                                100: Phone Number.
                                101: Computer.
                                102: Comment.

                USER:   String,   Used to store result, use at least 40 chars.

                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 14 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     USER$=Space$(80)
                CARRIER = M_getuserstr(102,USER$)



16)INSTRUCTION: M_newaccess


   SUMMARY:     Sets a new access level for the current user.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_newaccess(ACCESS)

                ACCESS: Integer,  New Access level to set.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 15 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     LOSER = 0
                CARRIER = M_newaccess(LOSER)



17)INSTRUCTION: M_addtime


   SUMMARY:     Adds extra time to current user's time, time can +/-.


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_addtime(TIME)

                TIME:   Integer,  Amount of time to add.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 21 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     WANKER = -20 
                CARRIER = M_addtime(WANKER)



18)INSTRUCTION: M_dofunction


   SUMMARY:     Performs a MAXS specific function. (MAXS specific)


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_dofunction(FUNC,EXTRA,PATH$)

                FUNC:   Integer,  Function number.
                EXTRA:  Integer,  Extra value for function.
                PATH$:  String,   Path value for function. 
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, function+100 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     DLOAD = 24 
                FILE$ = "BBS:Files\Files.list"
                CARRIER = M_dofunction(DLOAD,0,FILE$)



19)INSTRUCTION: M_changeuserdata


   SUMMARY:     Allows the changing of MAXS specific data for current user.
                Work out the "Types" yourselves >-]. (MAXS specific)


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_changeuserdata(TYPE,DATA)

                TYPE:   Integer,  Type of data to change.
                DATA:   Integer,  Data to change type to.
                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, 200 = success.


   EXAMPLE:     CARRIER = M_changeuserdata(0,100)



20)INSTRUCTION: M_getkey


   SUMMARY:     Gets a key instantly without waiting. (MAXS specific)


   USAGE:       RESULT = M_getkey

                RESULT: Integer,  20 = dropped carrier, keypress = $RXXXXXXX.
                                                        REMOTE   = $800000AA.
                                                        LOCAL    = $000000AA.

                                                        $  = HEX number.
                                                        R  = Remote bit.
                                                        AA = ASCII char.


   EXAMPLE:     KEY = M_getkey
                If (KEY And $80000000) = $80000000
                  CARRIER = M_bbstext("REMOTE Key = "+Str$(KEY And $000000FF))
                Else
                  CARRIER = M_bbstext("LOCAL Key = "+Str$(KEY And $000000FF))
                Endif
